   "models_label": "TTC-6 · TTC-8 · 2 models, C-axis versions",
   "summary": "The TTC is Dener's compact slant-bed CNC lathe for shaft, flange and bushing work in series: a one-piece cast bed inclined at 45° that sheds chips into the conveyor, roller linear guides and C1 / C3 ballscrews coupled straight to the servo motors, a spindle on super-precision bearings and a 12-station servo turret that indexes in 0.2 s. The TTC-6 turns parts to Ø12″ (305 mm) × 17″ (433 mm) behind a 6″ hydraulic chuck at 6,000 rpm and takes 1.77″ (45 mm) bar; the TTC-8 has an 8″ chuck, 2.05″ (52 mm) bar and 4,500 rpm. With the optional BMT55 C-axis turret and its 12 live tools the same machine drills, taps and mills flats and slots in the one setup. Fanuc 0i-TF Plus control as standard, Mitsubishi M80 to order.",
