   "models_label": "TMC 850 – TMC 1600 · 5 models",
   "summary": "Dener's TMC vertical machining centres mill, drill, bore and tap in one setup — pockets, contours, rigid tapping without a floating holder, and shapes drawn freehand in the Navi-Mill conversational software. The base, column and saddle are stress-relieved Meehanite castings laid out by finite-element analysis; the BBT40 spindle is direct-driven at 10,000 rpm (12,000 or 15,000 to order) with its own cooling; the 24-tool arm changer swaps tools in 1.3 s; double-nut C3 ballscrews and roller guides traverse at 1,417 in/min (36 m/min) and position to ±0.00016″ (±0.004 mm). Five sizes from the TMC 850 — 33.5 × 20.1 × 22″ (850 × 510 × 560 mm) over a 39 × 20″ table — to the TMC 1600 with 63 × 27.6 × 27.6″ (1,600 × 700 × 700 mm) and a 2,646 lb (1,200 kg) table load; the 1300 and 1600 have a 40 HP (30 kW) spindle motor.",
