   "models_label": "TDC 2112 · TDC 3116 · TDC 4120 · 3 models",
   "summary": "For parts too long, wide or heavy for a vertical machining centre — machine bases, moulds, plates, frames — the TDC double-column (gantry) machining centre carries the spindle on a saddle across a rigid cross rail between two columns, over a table that travels underneath. The BBT50 direct-drive spindle runs to 10,000 rpm on a 30 / 35 HP (22 / 26 kW) motor, with through-spindle coolant at 435 psi (30 bar); roller guides on all three axes. Three sizes: the TDC 2112 with 82.7 × 48 × 23.6″ (2,100 × 1,220 × 600 mm) travels, 55″ (1,400 mm) between the columns and a 24-tool changer, the TDC 3116 with 122 × 63 × 40″ and the TDC 4120 with 161 × 79.5 × 40″ (4,100 × 2,020 × 1,020 mm), a 157.5 × 71″ table for 26,455 lb (12,000 kg) and a 40-tool chain magazine.",
